{{review_baseline}}
Large requirement inputs (design, strategy, plan) are referenced by path and sha256 above rather than inlined. Read those files from the run directory.
Prior validation/review diagnostics (resolve any evidence-format errors in your own report): {{review_feedback}}
{{qa_gate}}
{{overwatch_review}}
A test that also fails on the unchanged base is not this change's defect: the check compares its failures with the base. Report a failing test as BLOCKING only when the change causes it. Leave the run's worktree as you found it: write scratch files outside it.
A numeric score, source inspection and requirement coverage are different evidence. The brief, accepted criteria/design and current user intent ledger are binding. Only explicit user changes or exclusions can alter them; an author, coordinator, reviewer or README cannot waive an ask. Missing required evidence is failed or unverified, never pending-but-passed. Do not modify the implementation. If a required tool/credential is unavailable, write `UNAVAILABLE:` with the dependency and exact unblock action; do not request recoding or unchanged retries.

